==Powers and Abilities==
<gallery type="slideshow">
BenAgain (337).png|Jackhammer Arms/Enhanced Digging
SD (381).png|Earthquake Generation (via Jackhammering)
SD (356).png|Fissure Generation (via Jackhammering)
Jackhammer Propulsion.png|Jackhammer Propulsion
RoE (217).png|Drill Formation
DepreyPresa1P356.png|Enhanced Strength
Malefactor (203.3).png|Shock Wave Generation (via Enhanced Strength)
The More Things Change, Part 2 (408).png|Enhanced Durability
Malefactor (210).png|Enhanced Acrobatics/Enhanced Agility and Reflexes
TToE_(172).png|Finger Retraction
SoY (375).png|Shock Wave Blender
</gallery>
Armodrillo's power comes from his forearms, which are embedded with biomechanical pneumatic pistons.{{Refn|group = AP|name = Armo}} They run from the hand, through the arm socket, and out the elbow, and can extend out of either side. By pumping them back and forth rapidly, Armodrillo can use them as biological jackhammers and rumble the earth around him with destructive vibrations,{{Refn|''[[Ben 10 Ultimate Alien: Power Struggle]]''; [[:File:PS DVD Armodrillo Data.png|file]]|group = DVD|name = Drillo}} creating tremors;<ref name="ATTWB">''[[And Then There Was Ben]]''</ref> fissures;<ref name="RG">''[[Reflected Glory]]''</ref><ref name="SD">''[[Special Delivery]]''</ref> and earthquakes.<ref name="SD" />{{Refn|group = AP|name = Armo}} [[Talpaedan|Talpaedans]] can also vibrate their own bodies with extreme precision, as [[Andreas]] was able to counter-vibrate his body to nearly completely nullify the impact of a sonic cannon that would have destroyed 5 square miles. Andreas' counter-vibration was also able to completely collapse a [[Forever Knights|Forever Knight]] castle building into rubble.<ref name="AF" />

Armodrillo can retract his fingers into his hand socket,<ref name="MOI">''[[Map of Infinity (Episode)|Map of Infinity]]''</ref><ref name="TToE">''[[The Transmogrification of Eunice]]''</ref> or morph his hands into spinning drills.<ref name="TToE" /><ref name="OPaPP2">''[[Of Predators and Prey: Part 2]]''</ref><ref name="Malefactor">''[[Malefactor]]''</ref><ref name="ROE">''[[Rules of Engagement]]''</ref> His mastery over the ground allows him to effortlessly dig tunnels deep in the ground;<ref name="BA" /><ref name="TSODS">''[[The Secret of Dos Santos]]''</ref>{{Refn|group = DVD|name = Drillo}} to the point that his species can glide through solid earth and rock as simply as [[Human (Classic)|Humans]] can walk through air.<ref name="TToE" /><ref name="SD" />{{Refn|group = AP|name = Armo}}

Armodrillo is incredibly strong, being able to lift a [[Mucilator|Mucilator]],<ref name="OPaPP1">''[[Of Predators and Prey: Part 1]]''</ref> hold his own against [[Trombipulor]] and launch him over several buildings,<ref name="SD" /> harm a [[Galilean]] with his drills,<ref>''[[For a Few Brains More]]''</ref> and destroy ten [[Computron's Minions|robots]] from [[Dimension 12]].<ref name="HT">''[[Hero Time]]''</ref> Additionally, he can generate shock waves that can destroy buildings from his sheer strength, as demonstrated by [[Ultimate Aggregor]].<ref name="UA">[[Ultimate Aggregor (Episode)|Ultimate Aggregor]]</ref><ref name="TFOC">''[[The Forge of Creation]]''</ref> Armodrillo can pump his pistons forward to further enhance the power of his punches;<ref name="Malefactor" /> pummel enemies; and batter buildings, even mountains, down to rubble.{{Refn|group = AP|name = Armo}} He can also do this to launch himself high in the air off the ground in a pinch;<ref name="OPaPP2" /> shoot objects in his grip forward like a cannon;<ref name="TMTCP2" /><ref name="IaMBW1">''[[It's a Mad, Mad, Mad Ben World: Part 1]]''</ref>  or extend the reach of his arms for a sudden and powerful shove, as demonstrated by [[Toolboxx]].<ref name="IaMBW1" />

Armodrillo possesses enhanced durability, courtesy of his armor. He is durable enough to withstand attacks from many powerful opponents, as well as being thrown through walls.<ref name="TMTCP2" /> Armodrillo is also immune to neuroshock blasts, as demonstrated by Andreas.<ref name="AF" />

Armodrillo is quite agile, being able to quickly roll out of the way of [[Slamworm]]'s attack.<ref name="Malefactor" />

Armodrillo is capable of rapidly spinning his drills to generate a continuous shock wave that effectively functions as a blender. This technique was used by [[Humungousaur (Classic)|Humungousaur]] with Armodrillo's arm (courtesy of [[Skurd]]) to completely disintegrate a tree.<ref>''[[Stuck on You]]''</ref>

==Weaknesses==
<gallery type="slideshow">
The More Things Change, Part 2 (420).png|Out-of-Control Vibration
Malefactor (241).png|Slammoid Predation
The More Things Change, Part 2 (440).png|Electricity Vulnerability
RotS (419).png|Suffocation
</gallery>
Certain weapons can cause Armodrillo's nervous system to go out of control and make him unable to stop vibrating his arm.<ref name="TMTCP2" />

Being a [[Talpaedan]], Armodrillo is at a massive disadvantage against a [[Slammoid]] due to them being able to easily dig him out of the ground,<ref name="OPaPP1" /><ref name="OPaPP2" /><ref name="Malefactor" /> their beak can find weaker joints to puncture his flesh, whereas acid projectiles can dissolve his armor entirely.{{Refn|[[:File:Slamworm Acid Spit.PNG]]|group = DJW|name = link}}

Armodrillo is vulnerable to electricity.<ref name="TMTCP2" />

Armodrillo can be rendered unconscious if he is hit by a quill from a member of [[Argit|Argit's]] [[Argit's Species|species]], as demonstrated with [[Andreas]].<ref name="AF" />

Armodrillo can be suffocated if a large amount of matter covers his whole body and compresses it enough.<ref>''[[Revenge of the Swarm]]''</ref>

==History==
===Ultimate Alien===
*In ''[[Andreas' Fault]]'', Armodrillo's DNA was sampled and put in the [[Codon Stream]] when the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]] scanned [[Andreas]]' DNA.
*Armodrillo first appeared in ''[[Hero Time]]'', where he helped [[Captain Nemesis]] defeat some of [[Computron]]'s [[Computron's Minions|minions]].
*In ''[[Reflected Glory]]'', Armodrillo battled some [[Forever Knights]].
*In ''[[...Nor Iron Bars a Cage]]'', Armodrillo battled [[Ultimate Kevin]].
*In ''[[The Transmogrification of Eunice]]'', Armodrillo rushed to save [[Eunice]] when he thought she was being attacked by a bear.
*In ''[[Revenge of the Swarm]]'', Armodrillo freed [[Julie Yamamoto|Julie]] and fought some [[Dr. Victor Valadis]] clones, but was defeated by [[Elena Valadis|Elena]].
*In ''[[The Creature From Beyond]]'', Armodrillo battled the victims of the [[Lucubra]]'s mind control before switching into [[NRG]].
*In ''[[Double or Nothing]]'', Armodrillo scared a ticket clerk to let him and [[Alien Force|the team]] into the theatre.
*In ''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]'', Armodrillo was seen confronting [[Albedo]] in a dream.

===Omniverse===
*In ''[[The More Things Change: Part 2]]'', Armodrillo defeated many of [[Psyphon]]'s [[Psyphon's Gang|henchmen]], but failed to defeat Psyphon himself.
*In ''[[Of Predators and Prey: Part 1]]'', Armodrillo was defeated by [[Slamworm]].
*In ''[[Of Predators and Prey: Part 2]]'', Armodrillo battled Slamworm and [[Crabdozer (Transformation)|Crabdozer]].
*In ''[[Malefactor]]'', Armodrillo battled Slamworm and Crabdozer again before switching into [[Big Chill (Classic)|Big Chill]].
*In ''[[Rules of Engagement]]'', Armodrillo failed to defeat [[Looma Red Wind|Princess Looma]].
*In ''[[Ben Again]]'', Armodrillo was used by 11-year-old [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] in 16-year-old Ben's body to find coordinates in the basement of [[Pakmar]]'s Fine Teas.
*In ''[[Special Delivery]]'', Armodrillo battled [[Zombozo (Classic)|Zombozo]], [[Fistrick]], and [[Trombipulor]].
*In'' [[The Ultimate Heist]]'', Armodrillo broke into [[Thirteen]]'s warehouse.
*In ''[[Return to Forever]]'', Armodrillo tried to break out of a force field, but was reverted by the [[Forever Knights]]' [[DNA Scanner]].
*In ''[[For a Few Brains More]]'', [[Albedo|Negative]] Armodrillo defeated [[Gravattack]] before switching into Negative Gravattack.
*In ''[[And Then There Was Ben]]'', [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]] as Armodrillo caused a small earthquake so a young Ben Prime could fall into the crater where the [[Omnitrix (Original)|original Omnitrix]] landed during the events of ''[[And Then There Were 10]]''.
*In ''[[Stuck on You]]'', [[Skurd]] gave [[Humungousaur (Classic)|Humungousaur]] Armodrillo's arm to battle [[Khyber]] as [[Tyrannopede]].
*In ''[[The Secret of Dos Santos]]'', Armodrillo tried to find the entrance to the Temple of the Sky until [[Kai Green|Kai]] did so herself.
*In ''[[Malgax Attacks]]'', Skurd gave [[Whampire]] Armodrillo's arm to battle [[Malware Armor|Mal]][[Vilgax (Classic)|gax]].
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Armodrillo appeared for a short time when Ben was cycling through his aliens.

