==Etymology==
Armodrillo's name is a combination of the words "armor", "drill", and "armadillo".

==Trivia==
*Armodrillo and the other [[Andromeda (Classic)|Andromeda]] aliens have their powers related to a basic element; for Armodrillo, it is earth.
*Armodrillo was the [[Alien of the Month]] in August 2011, though his name was misspelled as "Armadrillo".
*Armodrillo was designed by [[Steven Choi]] or [[Chap Yaep]].{{Refn|[[:File:Steven and Chap Andromeda.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Armodrillo and [[Ampfibian (Classic)|Ampfibian]] are the only Andromeda aliens in '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]''' to receive unique [[Transformation Sequences|transformation sequence]].
*Armodrillo first appeared in ''[[Tabloid Trouble]]'', a non-canon [[Comics|comic]] released concurrently to '''Ultimate Alien''', before his on-screen debut in ''[[Hero Time]]''.
*Armodrillo was originally intended to appear in ''[[The Perfect Girlfriend]]''. His role was taken by [[Echo Echo]] and [[Ultimate Echo Echo]] in the final version.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/7/75/Perfection_DRAFT-1.pdf ''Perfection'' Script First Draft]|group = script|name = draft1}}{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/2/26/The_Perfect_Girlfriend_DRAFT-2.pdf ''The Perfect Girlfriend'' Script Second Draft]|group = script|name = second}}
*Armodrillo was originally not supposed to appear in the dream in ''[[Night of the Living Nightmare]]''.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/d/d4/Night_of_the_Living_Nightmare_Script_First_Draft.pdf ''Night of the Living Nightmare'' Script First Draft]|group = script|name = first}}

